.TH nut-bios 1  "nut-cli 0.1.0" nut
.SH NAME
nut\-bios \- Guide and verify BIOS recovery settings
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBnut bios\fR [\fB\-\-color\fR] [\fB\-\-ascii\fR] [\fB\-j\fR|\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-c\fR|\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIsubcommands\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Guide and verify BIOS recovery settings
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<WHEN>\fR [default: auto]
Color output policy
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto
.IP \(bu 2
always
.IP \(bu 2
never
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-ascii\fR
Use ASCII symbols and bars
.TP
\fB\-j\fR, \fB\-\-json\fR
Emit machine\-readable JSON where supported
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Include additional diagnostic detail
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-config\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Read host settings from this file
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
nut\-bios\-guide(1)
Print a numbered keyboard walkthrough for this board
.TP
nut\-bios\-setup(1)
Reboot into firmware setup after a hostname interlock
.TP
nut\-bios\-attest(1)
Record a BIOS\-version\-pinned attestation receipt
.TP
nut\-bios\-profile(1)
List, show, or scaffold a board profile
